From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qcap: AVI mux audio and seeking, audio capture and capture graph pieces, WoW64 media type fix.

pieces, and a 32-bit V4L media type fix.

The AVI mux writes audio streams beside video, keeps master stream,
interleaving and index (idx1 optional) settings, writes an INFO list from
its IPersistMediaPropertyBag, implements IMediaSeeking as the tests show,
IAMStreamControl, IQualityControl and empty property pages. The audio
capture filter accepts PCM only, reports allocator properties, answers the
pin category property set, IAMFilterMiscFlags, and loads/saves WaveInId and
UseMixer through IPersistPropertyBag. The video capture filter saves its
VFWIndex, answers the pin category property set and IAMVideoControl
(no flip/trigger caps), and GetStreamCaps refuses an index equal to the
count. ICaptureGraphBuilder2 creates its graph lazily, SetOutputFileName
builds mux + file writer, ControlStream, AllocCapFile and CopyCaptureFile
work. File writer GetCurFile, smart tee QueryAccept, AVI compressor
InitNew/Save. The WoW64 thunk for media types left the 32-bit pUnk as
stack garbage, so enumerating a real webcam's types crashed 32-bit callers
in FreeMediaType; it is now cleared. Removes 47 todo_wine marks of the
avimux and smart tee tests.
The mux serialises its input pins (video and audio stream at once) and
writes audio as NNwb chunks.
